---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import CarvedDivider from "../components/CarvedDivider";

const title = "Ram Hanuman Connection — The Union of Master and Servant";
const description = "Explore the profound relationship between Lord Rama and Hanuman. Understand how Hanuman's devotion represents the pinnacle of Bhakti Yoga and selflessness.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="space-y-10 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    
    <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
    <nav class="text-xs text-charcoal-brown/50 font-semibold" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol class="list-none p-0 inline-flex gap-2">
        <li class="flex items-center">
          <a href="/" class="hover:text-maroon-deep">Home</a>
          <span class="mx-2">/</span>
        </li>
        <li class="text-maroon-deep truncate max-w-[200px]" aria-current="page">
          Ram Hanuman Connection
        </li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="text-center space-y-3">
      <span class="text-xs font-bold tracking-widest text-maroon-deep bg-marigold/30 px-3 py-1 rounded border border-marigold">
        Divine Relationship (स्वामी-सेवक भाव)
      </span>
      <h1 class="font-serif-display text-3xl uppercase tracking-wider font-bold text-maroon-deep">
        Shree Ram & Hanuman Connection
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-charcoal-brown/70 max-w-xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        Hanuman's devotion to Lord Rama is the highest expression of Bhakti (devotion). In Hindu theology, Hanuman is the bridge that leads the seeker to Lord Rama.
      </p>
    </div>

    <CarvedDivider icon="🕉️" />

    <!-- Main content grid -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 items-start">
      
      <!-- Detail text -->
      <div class="md:col-span-2 space-y-6 text-sm sm:text-base text-charcoal-brown/90 leading-relaxed">
        
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-serif-display text-lg font-bold text-maroon-deep uppercase border-b border-brass-gold/20 pb-2">
            The Essence of Dasya Bhakti (दास्य भक्ति)
          </h3>
          <p>
            In spiritual paths, there are various ways to connect with the Divine. Hanuman represents <i>Dasya Bhakti</i>—the devotion of a loving servant towards their master. This is not a relationship of subordination, but one of complete freedom and pure love.
          </p>
          <p>
            Hanuman surrendered his ego completely to Lord Rama. By having no separate desires of his own, he became a channel of infinite strength and cosmic intelligence. He accomplished tasks that even gods found impossible—like crossing the ocean or carrying the Dronagiri mountain.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-serif-display text-lg font-bold text-maroon-deep uppercase border-b border-brass-gold/20 pb-2">
            Why Hanuman Chants Rama's Name
          </h3>
          <p>
            It is said that Lord Hanuman is constantly immersed in the chanting of Rama's name (<i>Ram Naam Chanting</i>). For Hanuman, the name of Rama is more sweet and powerful than Rama himself.
          </p>
          <p>
            When Rama offered Hanuman any boon at the end of the Treta Yuga, Hanuman requested only one thing: to remain on Earth in physical form as long as the name of Rama is chanted by humans. This makes Hanuman a living, breathing immortal deity (Chiranjeevi) who protects devotees today.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-serif-display text-lg font-bold text-maroon-deep uppercase border-b border-brass-gold/20 pb-2">
            Chanting Rule: Rama First
          </h3>
          <p>
            Lord Hanuman is known as <i>Ram Doot</i> (the messenger of Rama). Devotees seeking the protection of Hanuman should always start by remembering Lord Rama. Chanting &ldquo;Jai Shree Ram&rdquo; before reading the Hanuman Chalisa immediately pleases Hanuman and invokes his protective presence.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="pt-4 border-t border-brass-gold/20 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
          <a
            href="/"
            class="bg-vermilion hover:bg-marigold text-stone-ivory hover:text-maroon-deep px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-xs font-bold uppercase border border-brass-gold shadow-sm transition-all duration-300"
          >
            Chant Hanuman Chalisa &rarr;
          </a>
          <a
            href="/shri-hanuman-chalisa-path-vidhi"
            class="bg-stone-ivory hover:bg-marigold/10 text-maroon-deep px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-xs font-bold uppercase border border-brass-gold/40 shadow-sm transition-all duration-300"
          >
            Learn Chanting Rules &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- Sidebar Panel -->
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div class="bg-stone-ivory border border-brass-gold/30 p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm space-y-4">
          <h4 class="font-serif-display text-sm uppercase tracking-wider font-bold text-maroon-deep border-b border-brass-gold/20 pb-2">
            Key Milestones
          </h4>
          
          <ul class="space-y-3 text-xs text-charcoal-brown/80 leading-relaxed">
            <li class="flex gap-2">
              <span>💍</span>
              <span><b>The Ring of Hope:</b> Hanuman located Sita in Ravana's Ashok Vatika, bringing her Rama's ring as a sign of hope.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-2">
              <span>⛰️</span>
              <span><b>The Sanjeevani Herb:</b> Hanuman carried an entire mountain to save Lakshmana, proving his resourcefulness.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-2">
              <span>🔥</span>
              <span><b>Burning of Lanka:</b> With his tail set on fire, Hanuman burned golden Lanka, shattering Ravana's pride.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- Ad Slot -->
        <div class="no-print w-full h-48 bg-stone-ivory border border-brass-gold/20 flex items-center justify-center text-xs text-charcoal-brown/40 tracking-widest uppercase rounded shadow-inner">
          Ad Slot — Sidebar
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>
</Layout>
